Z||000000||SloPonti||01-12-2000||12:29 AM||||A little leston learned by me today that i will share with you! About two months ago i started taking apart my car and i broke a part and i contacted my parts source fierodave and he could not help me so he referred me to someone else off this forum that does buisness here! i contacted him and he said he could do that for me plus i order some of his other parts! sent him the money very quickly and now two months later i still do not have the parts-which i need by this weekend so i can put the motor back together! tonight he emails me and says he is going to issue me a refund because he does not have the time to get me the parts! i feel that this is bad buisness especially for a fiero person! i have never waited this long for a part before and what really upsets me is that the motor will not be put in the car this weekend now because i need the parts! the lesson here is know who you are dealing with and make sure they have the parts on hand or a true estimate of time of how long it will take! i am not trying to start a fight here so don't reply with any bad posts but just a little note for everyone to remember when ordering! Thanks<BR>Rob<P>buy the way the part i need is the bracket that hold the automatic transmision to the four banger motor! if anyone has this piece let me know because i need it bad!!!<BR>thanks||||reg||9
